Subject: [PATCH] linkd: an unfilled answers placeholder is no firstboot.conf

Against derekross/omamobile-installer 53bd2f426455 (branch linkd-ffs, PR #15),
for omarchy-mobile's package omamobile-install-link until the daemon has it
itself (docs/INSTALL-LINK-PLAN.md §19, "for the daemon to change").

A release root image carries /etc/omamobile/firstboot.conf and
/etc/omamobile/boot-update.conf as placeholders: 4096 bytes of comment lines
that the desktop installer and the web page fill in place as they stream
the image (omarchy-mobile rootfs/placeholders, RELEASES §6.1). The plan's
decision of 2026-11-13 says "no firstboot.conf" in the start-up rules means
no file or the image's unfilled placeholder. The daemon tested existence
only, so on a link image whose placeholder nobody filled the first start
ended the link as `not-first-start` (§6.5 row 3) before it offered anything,
and a placeholder boot-update.conf counted as present, so the step that
writes it "if missing" left AUTO_WRITE off on a phone the link installed.

A file holds answers when it has a line that is neither blank nor a
comment, as omamobile-firstboot (0.1.6) and omamobile-boot-update read it.
One that exists and cannot be read counts as holding answers: the start-up
rules never take a phone for a first start on a guess.

tests/rows.rs: a first start with both placeholders is offered; a filled
placeholder is still not a first start; at stage `firstboot` a placeholder
boot-update.conf is written as a missing one is. The first fails without
the change to found.rs.

